XVaults:
X
XEventually, the player will encounter what is known as a treasure
Xvault. The vault is a 2x2 room, with four "$" spaces, and no doors.
There Xis always a secret door somewhere on a vault level which leads
to a space Xwhich teleports the user to the vault. There is always an
engraving which Xsays "ad ?ae??um." If you find this engraving,
search for the secret door Xnext to it.
X
XTo get out of a vault with all the money, you have to either teleport
Xor use a wand of digging. If you have neither, eventually a guard
will Xenter the vault. He is harmless, but will lead you out of the
vault if you Xare carrying NO money. Should you discover the answer
to his question, he Xwill leave by yourself in the vault. (In other
words, knowing the answer Xdoes not help). My luckiest move was
zapping a guard with a wand of Xpolymorph. He turned into a Quantum
Mechanic, hit me, and teleported me out. X
XNymphs:
X
XAlthough Nymphs can be annoying, they can do one extremely useful
Xthing: they can steal cursed items. Therefore, if a Nymph is found,
you Xcan use her to remove your cursed items. The way this is done is
demonstrated Xin the following example of how to check unidentified
rings with a Nymph on Xthe level.
X
X1) Clear out the level the Nymph is on.
X2) Go down to the next level, and clear it.
X3) Try putting on your unidentified rings. If a ring is not cursed,
X   name it something such as "uncursed1" to mark that this
X   type of ring is not cursed.
X4) Upon finding a cursed ring, remove ALL of your equipment, and drop
X   it on that space. Then go up the stairs, find the Nymph, and
X   let her steal an item. The item she steals then has to be
X   the cursed item. Go back down, equip yourself, and continue.
X
XNot using the dog:
X
XAlthough the dog seems to be a useful ally, in fact he presents a
good Xplayer with a handicap. This is for a number of reasons.
X1) Anything the dog kills, the character does not get experience for.
X   This means that it takes longer to go up levels while using the
dog. X2) The dog will eat edible monsters and other Comestibles that
the X   character needs. Hence, there is less food for the character.
X3) Perhaps the worst thing about the dog is that the user can NOT
enter X   the dog's space. This means that the dog can actually trap
the user X   in a corridor, and prevent the user's escape from a
powerful monster. XFor these reasons, unless you have the
uncontrollable urge to experiment with Xthe dog, it is best to leave
the dog behind on the first level. X
XCarry extra items, but don't carry gold:
X
XThe user should always carry as many items as he possibly can through
Xthe dungeon. This is because even worthless items can be polymorphed
or sold Xin the shops for gold. On the other hand, you should NEVER
carry gold. The Xgold weighs a non-negligible amount, and is not used
unless the person is Xbuying an item in a shop. Since buying items is
very rare, it is best to Xpile all the gold from a level next to the
stairs going up. That way, on the Xway back up, the winning player
can collect all the money he left behind. XBut, weight for weight,
the most valuable gem is worth many times more than Xthe gold you
could carry around. Bring rocks and polymorph them into gems. X
XOne useful technique of bringing more items than you can carry along
Xis to shuffle them down. Carry your items in two (or more) piles.
Leave one Xpile by the stairs, while carrying the other items. When
you find the stairs Xgoing down, drop the surplus items, go get the
other pile, and bring it down Xto the next level. Drop that pile, go
back up, and get the other items. XOr you could wear a ring of
leviatation and use that to go up the stairs. X
XFighting floating eyes:
X
XMany beginning players fight floating eyes by killing them in hand
Xto hand combat. This is not a very good method, since it lets the
eye get a Xchance to paralyze you. Instead, it is far preferable to
attack floating eyes Xby throwing weapons at them. If you have your
dog, you can always let the dog Xkill it, and then step in to eat the
eye before the dog gets a chance. X
XKilling Leprechauns:
X
XThe leprechaun is yet another reason not to carry any gold at all. If
Xyou are hit by a leprechaun while you have gold, not only do you
lose the Xgold (temporarily), but the trickster also teleports away,
and so you have Xto hunt him down. If you do not have any gold,
however, he is a very weak Xmonster worth gold and experience. Before
you fight one, drop your gold in a Xplace he can not get to, and then
kill him. Also be careful about letting Xthe leprechaun run away,
